  "model": "openhands/minimax-m2.7",
  "selected_user_text": "<pr_description>\nConsider the following PR description:\nBleach HTML serializer fails to produce any output\n### What happened?\n\nAfter recent changes to `BleachHTMLSerializer`, calling `.serialize()` returns nothing\u2014no HTML output is generated at all, regardless of input.\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\nThe serializer should return properly serialized HTML strings when processing a tree walker, just like before. Tags should be correctly rendered, attributes preserved (where allowed), and content properly escaped or passed through.\n\nInstead, it silently produces no output.\n\n### Minimal Complete Verifiable Example\n\n```python\nfrom bleach import clean\n\n# This should return a cleaned string with links and tags handled\nhtml = 'Check <a href=\"https://example.com\">this link</a> out!'\nresult = clean(html)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```html\nCheck <a href=\"https://example.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">this link</a> out!\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\n(nothing \u2014 empty string or None)\n```\n\nThis affects `clean`, `linkify`, and any function relying on HTML serialization.\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\n- All tests involving HTML output now fail silently or with type errors due to `None` being returned unexpectedly.\n- Appears to be related to the `BleachHTMLSerializer.serialize` method being effectively disabled.\n\n### Environment\n\n- bleach version: main (post-html5lib_shim changes)\n- Python: 3.8+\n- No external dependencies beyond standard test suite\n</pr_description>\n\n## Submission\nWhen you've completed your work (reading, editing, testing), and cannot make further progress\nissue exactly the following command:\n\necho COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT && git add -A && git diff --cached\n\nThis command will submit your work.\nYou cannot continue working (reading, editing, testing) in any way on this task after submitting.",
